.claude/

# Reference + documentation folders are kept local only.
# They contain proprietary diagrams, credential reference files, vendor
# specs, and internal architecture notes that shouldn't ship with the
# code. Anything that needs to be public-facing belongs in README files
# inside the relevant code package, not these folders.
reference/
docs/
# Exception: server/docs/ holds the canonical architecture .md that
# downstream views (Operations Manual wiki seed + How Brain Works
# visual page) derive from. Must ship with the deployment artifact.
!server/docs/
!server/docs/**

# Per-tenant Meta WhatsApp session — explicitly extra layer beyond the
# whatsapp-sessions/ rule above; some tooling lives in subdirs.
server/whatsapp-user-sessions/

# Stray local-only working dirs (not part of the project source)
Required\ Architect/

# Tenant phone session data + auth artifacts
**/whatsapp-sessions/
**/whatsapp-user-sessions/

# Retained local history from the removed orch pipeline (kept on disk, never committed)
crs/
logs/

# Owner-owned, never committed (AGENTS.md)
server/docs/nexeo_self_learning&development.md

# Build-output backups. `dist/` is already ignored, but a timestamped copy of it
# is not, so server/dist.bak-20260812-140334 put ~2600 compiled files into Source
# Control and VS Code reported "2664 changes". Nothing references it and
# `npm run build` regenerates dist from source, so a backup of it is never an
# artefact worth versioning — it is only a hazard: one `git add -A` away from a
# 19 MB commit, and AGENTS.md forbids that add for exactly this reason (BLD-001,
# where a directory add committed an owner-owned file).
#
# Widened 2026-08-31 from `dist.bak-*` to any `dist.*` sibling: the deploy path
# also writes `server/dist.pre-<sha>.<ts>/`, and four of those put 10,362 files
# into Source Control. VS Code caps its decoration provider at 10,000 events, so
# the git provider logged "CAPPING events from decorations provider vscode.git
# 10003" on every extension-host start and starved the Claude Code webview into
# rendering blank. Ignoring the prefix alone would leave the next prefix to
# rediscover this, so ignore the class: any sibling copy of the build output.
dist.*/
server/dist.*/

# Editor settings are per-machine, not per-project.
.vscode/

# Harvested production conversations — real message bodies, never committed.
server/docs/orchestrator/state/recent-chats.md
node_modules
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Orchestrator run artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The campaign loop regenerates all of this on every iteration: run logs, a
# per-iteration score card, ~40 scratch files of watermarks/hashes/session ids,
# and a `retired-*` archive each time a campaign is reset. Together that is
# ~4.2 MB across 150+ paths, and it has never been committed — only left
# uncommitted, which is the same hazard the dist.bak block above describes: one
# `git add -A` away from a junk commit, and AGENTS.md forbids that add for
# exactly this reason (BLD-001). It also floods Source Control, which is what
# the decoration-provider cap above is about.
#
# IGNORED, NOT DELETED. The retired-* archives and the ledger are the only
# record of past campaign resets, and `state/` holds live loop state — deleting
# them destroys history nothing else holds and would interrupt a running loop.
# They stay on disk; they just stop being git's business.
#
# Deliberately still TRACKED, because the campaign and the evaluation chart read
# them as current pointers rather than as run output: state/campaign.json,
# state/capability_scorecard.json, state/deployed-sha, state/builder-session-id,
# and scores/proactive-iter-*.json (cited by evaluation chart §2.2 and §2.3).
# The negations below say so out loud, so the next reset does not re-litigate it.
server/docs/orchestrator/*.log
server/docs/orchestrator/*.out
server/docs/orchestrator/ledger.jsonl
server/docs/orchestrator/orchestrator_ledger.md
server/docs/orchestrator/retired-*/
server/docs/orchestrator/scores/iter-*.json
server/docs/orchestrator/state/*
!server/docs/orchestrator/state/builder-session-id
!server/docs/orchestrator/state/campaign.json
!server/docs/orchestrator/state/capability_scorecard.json
!server/docs/orchestrator/state/deployed-sha
